, "created_at": "2026-11-09T04:36:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119650353142747181"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Most of the changes I make to my projects these days come in the form of PRs opened for me by Claude Code or Codex. The PR is my unit …", "display_url": "simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/9/det…", "end": 286, "expanded_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/9/details-summary/", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119650396390215680/rjJ3KynL?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119650396390215680/rjJ3KynL?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 263, "status": 200, "title": "Hide your slop PR descriptions behind", "unwound_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/9/details-summary/", "url": "https://t.co/JlFdAJovFt"}]}, "id": "2119650353142747181", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1157, "impression_count": 118844, "like_count": 1721, "quote_count": 65, "reply_count": 366, "retweet_count": 68}, "text": "I've recently started hiding the bulk of my AI-generated GitHub PR descriptions behind a collapsed &lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt; HTML tag (thankfully supported by GitHub Markdown) and I think it's a useful pattern for making PR slop a little bit less exhausting https://t.co/JlFdAJovFt", "url": "https://x.com/simonw/status/2119650353142747181"}, {"author_id": "985281530070265862", "created_at": "2026-11-08T23:30:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119573238456127692"], "id": "2119573238456127692", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 311, "impression_count": 228337, "like_count": 1798, "quote_count": 23, "reply_count": 115, "retweet_count": 61}, "text": "Nothing will happen to Jensen over the next 6 months, this story will largely die down in media / finance\nBut Democrats will call him into Congress\nThey will investigate the fuck out of GPU sales to Chinese companies\nAnd hammer him w questions\nThat's when the shoe /could/ drop", "ur